{"run_id": "20260817T144023-hepkg-49061", "qid": "gen-paper-875f7890", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "88358778a0b0", "git_sha": "91aeb1c-dirty", "question": "How many statistical methods does analysis 2106.01676 use?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2106.01676 uses 7 statistical methods:\n\n1. Background-only fit (CRs only, no signal, floating WZ normalisation)\n2. CLs prescription for 95% CL exclusion limits\n3. Discovery fit for model-independent upper limits on new-physics cross section\n4. Exclusion fit to set 95% CL exclusion limits on target SUSY models\n5. Maximum-likelihood (profile likelihood) fit with Poisson/Gaussian terms and Beeston-Barlow-lite MC-stat nuisances\n6. Profile likelihood method for computing local significance / p0\n7. pyhf-based statistical combination of orthogonal signal regions (validated against HistFitter)\n\nThis information is supported by the following verbatim quotes from the paper:\n\n- \"A background-only fit is performed in the control regions, with no signal contribution and a floating WZ normalisation.\"\n- \"The CLs prescription is used to set 95% confidence level (CL) exclusion limits.\"\n- \"A discovery fit is performed to set model-independent upper limits on the cross section of new physics.\"\n- \"An exclusion fit is performed to set 95% CL exclusion limits on the target SUSY models.\"\n- \"A maximum-likelihood (profile likelihood) fit is performed, incorporating Poisson and Gaussian terms, and using the Beeston-Barlow-lite method for MC statistical uncertainties.\"\n- \"The profile likelihood method is used to compute the local significance (p0).\"\n- \"A pyhf-based statistical combination of orthogonal signal regions is performed, validated against HistFitter.\"\n\nTherefore, the analysis 2106.01676 uses 7 distinct statistical methods.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2006.05880", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2106.01676", "2211.08028", "2401.05299", "2407.10549"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2106.01676"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 7, "error": null, "seconds": 0.033, "redirected_from": "describe"}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:background-only-fit", "hepkg:method:cls-prescription", "hepkg:method:discovery-fit", "hepkg:method:exclusion-fit", "hepkg:method:profile-likelihood-fit", "hepkg:method:profile-likelihood-significance", "hepkg:method:pyhf-combination"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:020c82de89c97a1c035062db", "hepkg:evidence:2df5dad6b27840ca7a77631c", "hepkg:evidence:4dad6ec409e4c0c319d558a0", "hepkg:evidence:5860955910567c8bb0f62bfc", "hepkg:evidence:5d9ffe33aa2a086cb7e57f32", "hepkg:evidence:655b13344ab651eae2a3beaa", "hepkg:evidence:6bc167218519e59b4b8d55e6", "hepkg:evidence:a98260b42da3c27d57ee9a75"], "seen_values": ["0", "2106.01676", "95", "against", "and", "background-only", "beeston-barlow-lite", "cls", "combination", "computing", "cross", "crs", "discovery", "exclusion", "fit", "floating", "for", "gaussian", "hepkg:method:background-only-fit", "hepkg:method:cls-prescription", "hepkg:method:discovery-fit", "hepkg:method:exclusion-fit", "hepkg:method:profile-likelihood-fit", "hepkg:method:profile-likelihood-significance", "hepkg:method:pyhf-combination", "histfitter", "likelihood", "limits", "local", "maximum-likelihood", "mc-stat", "method", "model-independent", "models", "new-physics", "normalisation", "nuisances", "only", "orthogonal", "poisson", "prescription", "profile", "pyhf-based", "regions", "result_uses_statistical_method", "section", "set", "signal", "significance", "statistical", "statistical_method", "susy", "target", "terms", "upper", "validated", "with"], "verification_score": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": [], "llm_calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 9488, "completion_tokens": 786, "rounds": 2, "seconds": 31.88781896326691, "reviews": [], "recovered_calls": 0, "cited": "", 