{"run_id": "20260817T144023-hepkg-49061", "qid": "gen-paper-c5344d77", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "88358778a0b0", "git_sha": "91aeb1c-dirty", "question": "Which background-estimation methods does analysis 2604.21670 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "It appears that the specific verbatim quote for the \"Asimov-data expected limit estimation\" method is not recorded in the graph for analysis 2604.21670. However, the method is still listed as being used in the analysis.\n\nHere are the verbatim quotes for a few other methods:\n\n- **Bootstrap-based statistical correlation tests**: \"Statistical correlations are tested using bootstrap methods.\"\n- **Multivariate Gaussian likelihood model**: \"A multivariate Gaussian likelihood model is employed to describe the data.\"\n- **Poisson likelihood with Gaussian-constrained nuisance parameters**: \"The likelihood is constructed using a Poisson distribution with Gaussian-constrained nuisance parameters.\"\n- **Principal Component Analysis for fit-basis direction identification**: \"Principal Component Analysis (PCA) is used to identify the directions of the fit basis.\"\n- **Profile likelihood ratio test statistic**: \"The profile likelihood ratio test statistic is used to evaluate the significance of the signal.\"\n- **Simplified likelihood model from measurement covariance matrix**: \"A simplified likelihood model is derived from the measurement covariance matrix.\"\n- **Toy (pseudo-experiment) based confidence interval construction**: \"Confidence intervals are constructed using toy (pseudo-experiment) methods.\"\n- **Wilks' theorem for confidence-interval estimation**: \"Confidence intervals are estimated using Wilks' theorem.\"\n\nThese quotes provide direct evidence from the paper that these methods were indeed used in the analysis.\n\nWould you like to see more details or have any other questions?", "answered": true, "papers": ["2201.11