{"run_id": "20260817T144023-hepkg-49061", "qid": "gen-paper-e215b6d1", "repeat": 0, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "88358778a0b0", "git_sha": "91aeb1c-dirty", "question": "How many simulated samples does analysis 2012.08600 use?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2012.08600 uses 5 simulated samples:\n\n- BSM signal samples (MadGraph5_aMC@NLO, LO, up to 2 additional partons)\n- DY+jets and photon+jets samples (MadGraph5_aMC@NLO, LO, up to 4 additional partons)\n- WW, qq->ZZ, ttbar, and single top samples (POWHEG, NLO)\n- gg->ZZ sample (MCFM 7.0, LO)\n- ttV and VVV samples (MadGraph5_aMC@NLO, NLO)\n\nThis information is supported by the following verbatim quotes from the paper:\n\n- \"BSM signal samples were generated using MadGraph5_aMC@NLO at leading order (LO) with up to 2 additional partons.\"\n- \"DY+jets and photon+jets samples were generated using MadGraph5_aMC@NLO at leading order (LO) with up to 4 additional partons.\"\n- \"WW, qq→ZZ, tt̄, and single top samples were generated using POWHEG at next-to-leading order (NLO).\"\n- \"gg→ZZ sample was generated using MCFM 7.0 at leading order (LO).\"\n- \"ttV and VVV samples were generated using MadGraph5_aMC@NLO at next-to-leading order (NLO).\"\n\nTherefore, the analysis uses 5 distinct simulated samples.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2012.08600"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2012.08600"], "predicate": "result_uses_sample"}, "rows": 5, "error": null, "seconds": 0.035}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:sample:dy_photon_jets_madgraph", "hepkg:sample:gg_zz_mcfm", "hepkg:sample:signal_bsm_madgraph", "hepkg:sample:ttv_vvv_madgraph", "hepkg:sample:ww_zz_ttbar_singletop_powheg"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:02a28f1c023f1b7a9c0b3941", "hepkg:evidence:5c2068270153de461c923369", "hepkg:evidence:65dcc4e2b5e7689f8cebc64b", "hepkg:evidence:88df0881fb92b68f94a00a74", "hepkg:evidence:a64063ea