{"run_id": "20260817T144023-hepkg-49061", "qid": "gen-paper-43cc1ae8", "repeat": 1, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "88358778a0b0", "git_sha": "91aeb1c-dirty", "question": "How many simulated samples does analysis 2007.02873 use?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The graph does not contain information about the simulated samples used in analysis 2007.02873.", "answered": false, "papers": [], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2007.02879"]}, "rows": 0, "error": null, "seconds": 0.177}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": [], "evidence_ids": [], "seen_values": [], "verification_score": 0.0, "unsupported_claims": ["2007.02873"], "llm_calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 8922, "completion_tokens": 177, "rounds": 2, "seconds": 7.269264400005341, "reviews": [], "recovered_calls": 0, "cited": "", "abstention_challenged": false, "citation_corrected": false, "citation_disagrees": [], "invented_ids": [], "nudged": false, "error": ""}, "scores": {"seconds": 7.269264400005341, "llm_calls": 2.0, "tokens": 9099.0, "rounds": 2.0, "errored": 0.0, "answered": 0.0, "abstained": 1.0, "refused_in_text": 1.0, "refusal_flag_disagrees": 0.0, "faithfulness": 0.0, "unsupported_claims": 1.0, "count_correct": 0.0, "tool_calls": 1.0, "tool_errors": 0.0, "tool_error_rate": 0.0, "retrieved_first": 1.0, "entities_retrieved": 0.0, "evidence_quotes": 0.0}}
{"run_id": "20260817T144023-hepkg-49061", "qid": "gen-paper-43db3120", "repeat": 1, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "88358778a0b0", "git_sha": "91aeb1c-dirty", "question": "How many quantities does analysis 2004.01678 report?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2004.01678 reports 22 distinct quantities. These include upper limits on the production cross section times branching ratio for \\(H \\rightarrow Z\\alpha\\) at various masses of \\(\\alpha\\), the expected and observed signal yields, the total background uncertainty, and the data-driven background estimate in the signal region. \n\nHere are some examples of the quantities reported:\n\n- 95% CL upper limit on \\(\\sigma(pp \\rightarrow H) \\times B(H \\rightarrow Za)\\) for \\(\\alpha\\) masses ranging from 0.5 GeV to 4.0 GeV.\n- Expected and observed 95% CL upper limits for \\(H \\rightarrow Z\\eta_c\\) and \\(H \\rightarrow ZJ/\\psi\\).\n- Total background uncertainty in the signal region: 3700 events.\n- Data-driven background estimate in the signal region: 82400 events.\n- Observed data yield in the signal region: 82908 events.\n\nEach of these quantities is supported by verbatim quotes from the paper. For example, the 95% CL upper limit on \\(\\sigma(pp \\rightarrow H) \\times B(H \\rightarrow Za)\\) for \\(\\alpha\\) mass of 0.5 GeV is reported as 17 pb (observed) with an expected range of 16 \\(\\pm\\) 5 (up) \\(\\pm\\) 6 (down) pb.\n\nThis analysis provides a comprehensive set of results, covering multiple signal hypotheses and detailed background estimates.", "answered": true, "papers": [], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2004.01678"], "predicate": "result_reports_quantity"}, "rows": 21, "error": null, "seconds": 0.051, "redirected_from": "describe"}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": [], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:02d1f455fea71f833136c037", "hepkg:evidence:138bdc46c4039abf6252