{"run_id": "20260817T144023-hepkg-49061", "qid": "gen-paper-7ff98823", "repeat": 1, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "88358778a0b0", "git_sha": "91aeb1c-dirty", "question": "How many statistical methods does analysis 2605.14245 use?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2605.14245 uses the following statistical methods:\n\n- CMS Combine statistical analysis tool\n- Discrete profiling method for data-driven background modeling (this is a background method, but it was listed under the statistical method predicate)\n- F-test for optimal function/order selection (signal Gaussian sum and background functions)\n- Goodness-of-fit test using the saturated model test statistic\n- Likelihood-ratio confidence interval definition under Wilks' theorem violation (-2ΔlnL<1,4)\n- Simultaneous extended maximum likelihood fit to diphoton mass spectrum\n\nTherefore, the analysis uses **6** statistical methods.\n\nHere is the evidence for each method:\n- CMS Combine statistical analysis tool: \"CMS Combine statistical analysis tool\"\n- Discrete profiling method for data-driven background modeling: \"Discrete profiling method for data-driven background modeling\"\n- F-test for optimal function/order selection: \"F-test for optimal function/order selection (signal Gaussian sum and background functions)\"\n- Goodness-of-fit test using the saturated model test statistic: \"Goodness-of-fit test using the saturated model test statistic\"\n- Likelihood-ratio confidence interval definition under Wilks' theorem violation: \"Likelihood-ratio confidence interval definition under Wilks' theorem violation (-2ΔlnL<1,4)\"\n- Simultaneous extended maximum likelihood fit to diphoton mass spectrum: \"Simultaneous extended maximum likelihood fit to diphoton mass spectrum\"\n\nAnswering the question based on the retrieved rows.\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"Analysis 2605.14245 uses 6 statistical methods: CMS Combine statistical analysis tool, Discrete profiling method for data-driven background modeling, F-test for optimal function/order selection, Goodness-of-fit test using the saturated model test statistic, Likelihood-ratio confidence interval definition under Wilks' theorem violation, and Simultaneous extended maximum likelihood fit to diphoton mass spectrum.\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}}\n</tool_call>", "answered": true, "papers": ["2605.14245"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2605.14245"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 6, "error": null, "seconds": 0.033, "redirected_from": "describe"}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:cms_combine_tool", "hepkg:method:discrete_profiling", "hepkg:method:extended_max_likelihood_fit", "hepkg:method:f_test_signal_background", "hepkg:method:saturated_model_gof", "hepkg:method:wilks_theorem_violation_ci"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:0640a6e7ff1b8d0f8974c824", "hepkg:evidence:1742681158db7cf5bb4574c6", "hepkg:evidence:1f6133f616cfb6b2b04149c0", "hepkg:evidence:383af97efe5f0e3df2fef35f", "hepkg:evidence:3a782e4d53616f87e51f3878", "hepkg:evidence:5a962e75c5c82babd762b778", "hepkg:evidence:70afca57a4e765759341e961", "hepkg:evidence:d4694a1e1ff8704f257d78bd", "hepkg:evidence:e02b65bcf36351ea951ecda0"], "seen_values": ["1,4", "14", "2", "2605.14245", "analysis", "and", "background", "background_method", "cms", "combine", "confidence", "data-driven", "definition", "diphoton", "discrete", "extended", "f-test", "fit", "for", "function", "functions", "gaussian", "goodness-of-fit", "hepkg:method:cms_combine_tool", "hepkg:method:discrete_profiling", "hepkg:method:extended_max_likelihood_fit", "hepkg:method:f_test_signal_background", "hepkg:method:saturated_model_gof", "hepkg:method:wilks_theorem_violation_ci", "interval", "likelihood", "likelihood-ratio", "lnl", "mass", "maximum", "method", "model", "modeling", "optimal", "or