{"run_id": "20260817T144023-hepkg-49061", "qid": "gen-paper-9264dc2e", "repeat": 1, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "88358778a0b0", "git_sha": "91aeb1c-dirty", "question": "How many systematic uncertainties does analysis 2106.14246 report?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2106.14246 reports 21 distinct systematic uncertainties. Here they are:\n\n- Charge (sign) misidentification background normalization uncertainty\n- Hadronic tau (tau_h) identification efficiency uncertainty\n- Integrated luminosity uncertainty\n- Jet energy scale and resolution uncertainty\n- Jet energy scale/resolution uncertainty for CMS fast simulation (signal)\n- Light lepton (e/mu) identification and isolation efficiency uncertainty\n- Multiboson (WWW/WWZ/WZZ/ZZZ) background normalization uncertainty\n- Nonprompt lepton (e/mu/tau_h) background normalization uncertainty\n- PDF uncertainty (NNPDF3.0/3.1 replicas)\n- Photon conversion (Zg) process normalization uncertainty\n- Pile-up reweighting modelling uncertainty\n- Renormalization and factorization scale uncertainty\n- Signal initial-state radiation (ISR) reweighting uncertainty\n- Signal p_T^miss modeling uncertainty (fast simulation)\n- Trigger efficiency uncertainty\n- WZ M_T/p_T^miss shape uncertainty derived from Wg control sample\n- WZ process normalization uncertainty\n- ZZ process normalization uncertainty\n- b tagging efficiency and misidentification correction uncertainty\n- b tagging efficiency uncertainty for CMS fast simulation (signal)\n- ttX background normalization uncertainty\n\nThis list is based on the systematic uncertainties explicitly recorded in the graph for this analysis.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.14060", "2012.01581", "2103.04956", "2106.14246"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2106.14246"], "predicate": "result_has_systematic"}, "rows": 21, "error": null, "seconds": 0.054, "re