{"run_id": "20260817T144023-hepkg-49061", "qid": "gen-paper-9ec710c4", "repeat": 1, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "88358778a0b0", "git_sha": "91aeb1c-dirty", "question": "Which background-estimation methods does analysis 2206.09466 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2206.09466 uses the following background-estimation methods:\n\n- Background determined from MC simulation only (no dedicated data-driven normalisation)\n- Data-driven misidentification/prompt-rate (fake rate) method\n- Data-driven sideband/Z-peak extrapolation technique\n- Data-embedding technique (muon replacement)\n- Data-to-simulation scale factor derived in a control region\n- Free-floating normalization constrained by dedicated control regions in the fit\n\nAnd the following statistical methods:\n\n- Binned maximum likelihood fit with log-normal constrained nuisance parameters\n- LHC Higgs Combination Group statistical approach\n- Profile likelihood ratio method\n\nThese methods are recorded in the graph as the techniques used by the analysis.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2006.05880", "2009.04363", "2206.09466"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2206.09466"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 3, "error": null, "seconds": 0.032}, {"round": 2, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2206.09466"], "predicate": "background_uses_method"}, "rows": 6, "error": null, "seconds": 0.038}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:binned-maximum-likelihood-fit", "hepkg:method:cr-constrained-fit-normalization", "hepkg:method:data-driven-fake-rate", "hepkg:method:data-driven-sideband-extrapolation", "hepkg:method:data-embedding", "hepkg:method:data-to-sim-scale-factor", "hepkg:method:lhc-higgs-combination-approach", "hepkg:method:mc-simulation-only", "hepkg:method:profile-likelihood"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:03c87d37d632246ab7ce857e", "hepkg: