{"run_id": "20260817T144023-hepkg-49061", "qid": "gen-paper-1a4b7e48", "repeat": 2, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "88358778a0b0", "git_sha": "91aeb1c-dirty", "question": "How many quantities does analysis 2508.13900 report?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2508.13900 reports 23 distinct quantities. These include mass limits, upper mass reaches, and other measures for various supersymmetric particles and processes, as well as a post-fit z-score distribution standard deviation. Each quantity is associated with specific conditions and values, such as mass differences and confidence levels.\n\nHere are some examples of the quantities reported:\n- Most stringent 95% CL lower mass limits for selectron (RR, LL, both) at Δm ~ 5 GeV: 160, 230, 250 GeV\n- Slepton masses excluded at 95% CL or higher (three chirality cases: RR-only, LL-only, both) for Δm range 3-80 GeV: 110, 175, 200 GeV\n- T2bW most stringent exclusion Δm range\n- Number of control-region bins out of total 2443 fit bins: 648 bins (62% of total)\n- Slepton (both L/R mass degenerate) upper mass reach at favorable Δm ~ 5 GeV: 270 GeV\n- T2bW upper mass reach: 620 GeV\n- T2tt (stop→t χ10) upper mass reach at Δm=150 GeV: 780 GeV\n- Post-fit z-score distribution standard deviation relative to expected unity: 1.12\n\nThese quantities provide a comprehensive overview of the results and constraints derived from the analysis.\n\nAnswer: Analysis 2508.13900 reports 23 distinct quantities. The graph supports this answer with the specific quantities and their values.", "answered": true, "papers": [], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2508.13900"], "predicate": "result_reports_quantity"}, "rows": 25, "error": null, "seconds": 0.054, "redirected_from": "describe"}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": [], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:0d7c81827531e445d0913176", "hepkg:evidence:27a12da67bd39848d16dd0fc", "