{"run_id": "20260817T144023-hepkg-49061", "qid": "gen-paper-254f151f", "repeat": 2, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "88358778a0b0", "git_sha": "91aeb1c-dirty", "question": "How many background-estimation methods does analysis 2401.07090 use?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2401.07090 uses 7 statistical methods for background estimation:\n\n- Data blinding procedure\n- Data-driven tag-and-probe method for reconstruction efficiency\n- Kernel density estimator (KDE) background templates\n- Profile likelihood confidence interval\n- Pseudo-experiments (used for uncertainty estimation)\n- Simultaneous unbinned maximum likelihood fit across 15 \\( q^2 \\) bins\n- Unbinned maximum likelihood fit\n\nThese methods are recorded in the graph as being used in this analysis.\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"Analysis 2401.07090 uses 7 statistical methods for background estimation:\\n\\n- Data blinding procedure\\n- Data-driven tag-and-probe method for reconstruction efficiency\\n- Kernel density estimator (KDE) background templates\\n- Profile likelihood confidence interval\\n- Pseudo-experiments (used for uncertainty estimation)\\n- Simultaneous unbinned maximum likelihood fit across 15 \\( q^2 \\) bins\\n- Unbinned maximum likelihood fit\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}", "answered": true, "papers": ["2112.00895", "2207.12246", "2401.07090", "2408.03744"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2401.07090"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 7, "error": null, "seconds": 0.034}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:data_blinding", "hepkg:method:kde", "hepkg:method:profile_likelihood", "hepkg:method:pseudo_experiments", "hepkg:method:simultaneous_fit", "hepkg:method:tag_and_probe", "hepkg:method:unbinned_ml_fit"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:1fef1d9b0ad95dbc952f0d79", "hepkg:evi