{"run_id": "20260817T144023-hepkg-49061", "qid": "gen-paper-6c16e3bd", "repeat": 2, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "88358778a0b0", "git_sha": "91aeb1c-dirty", "question": "How many statistical methods does analysis 2205.05120 use?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2205.05120 uses the following 5 statistical methods:\n\n1. Asymptotic approximation for CL$_{s}$ computation in model-dependent fits\n2. Barlow-Beeston method for limited simulation/control-region sample size\n3. Binned maximum likelihood fit combining all categories, channels, and data-taking years\n4. External constraints on nuisance parameters (log-normal for normalization, Gaussian for shape)\n5. Pseudoexperiments used to evaluate look-elsewhere/fluctuation probability and significance\n\nThese methods were identified from the paper's content. \n\nAnswer: 5 statistical methods.\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"Analysis 2205.05120 uses 5 statistical methods: Asymptotic approximation for CL$_{s}$ computation in model-dependent fits, Barlow-Beeston method for limited simulation/control-region sample size, Binned maximum likelihood fit combining all categories, channels, and data-taking years, External constraints on nuisance parameters (log-normal for normalization, Gaussian for shape), and Pseudoexperiments used to evaluate look-elsewhere/fluctuation probability and significance.\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}}\n</tool_call>", "answered": true, "papers": ["2205.05120", "2307.01094"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2205.05120"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 5, "error": null, "seconds": 0.044, "redirected_from": "describe"}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:statmethod:asymptotic-approximation", "hepkg:statmethod:barlow-beeston", "hepkg:statmethod:binned-maximum-likelihood-fit", "hepkg:statmethod:nuis