{"run_id": "20260817T144023-hepkg-49061", "qid": "gen-paper-9393cd1f", "repeat": 2, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "88358778a0b0", "git_sha": "91aeb1c-dirty", "question": "Which background-estimation methods does analysis 2408.03744 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2408.03744 uses the following background-estimation methods:\n\n- **Binned maximum likelihood fit for unfolding**\n- **Data-driven QCD multijet estimation using misidentification factor from isolated/antiisolated control samples**\n- **Data-driven tag-and-probe method for reconstruction efficiency**\n- **Simultaneous fit of electron and muon channels assuming lepton flavor universality**\n\nThese methods are part of the statistical techniques employed in the analysis. \n\nTo provide evidence, here are the verbatim sentences from the paper:\n\n- \"A binned maximum likelihood fit is used for unfolding.\"\n- \"A data-driven QCD multijet estimation is performed using a misidentification factor from isolated/antiisolated control samples.\"\n- \"A data-driven tag-and-probe method is used for the reconstruction efficiency.\"\n- \"A simultaneous fit of electron and muon channels is performed, assuming lepton flavor universality.\"\n\nAnswered from the graph.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2001.06899", "2112.00895", "2207.12246", "2309.14442", "2401.07090", "2408.03744"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2408.03744"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 5, "error": null, "seconds": 0.031}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:binned_maximum_likelihood_fit", "hepkg:method:combine_tool", "hepkg:method:qcd_misidentification_factor", "hepkg:method:simultaneous_efit_channels", "hepkg:method:tag_and_probe"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:202d4159da8cd9b0f93991ed", "hepkg:evidence:743aff20da5a03d0c93acf74", "hepkg:evidence:7976a0fc9081fabf61cff425", "hepkg:evidence