{"run_id": "20260817T144023-hepkg-49061", "qid": "gen-paper-b739c2ad", "repeat": 2, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "88358778a0b0", "git_sha": "91aeb1c-dirty", "question": "How many systematic uncertainties does analysis 2407.10549 report?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2407.10549 reports 12 systematic uncertainties. Here they are:\n\n- $E_T^{miss}$ trigger efficiency, energy scale and resolution uncertainty (found negligible)\n- $V\\\\!+\\\\!\\\\mathrm{jets}$ matching parameter and resummation scale uncertainty\n- $V\\\\!+\\\\!\\\\mathrm{jets}$ normalization uncertainty\n- $Z\\\\!+\\\\!\\\\mathrm{jets}$ modeling uncertainty\n- $b$-jet identification algorithm calibration uncertainty\n- $tW$ channel interference with $t\\\\bar{t}$ production uncertainty (diagram subtraction scheme)\n- Integrated luminosity uncertainty\n- Jet energy scale (JES) and jet energy resolution (JER) uncertainty\n- Jet mass scale (JMS) uncertainty for large-$R$ jets\n- Lepton identification efficiency uncertainty (found negligible)\n- Matrix element and parton shower generator choice uncertainty\n- PDF choice and factorization/renormalization scale uncertainty\n\nEach of these uncertainties is documented in the paper, and the labels provide a clear description of what each systematic uncertainty entails.\n\nAnswer: The analysis 2407.10549 reports 12 systematic uncertainties.\nAnswerable: True\nReason: answered", "answered": true, "papers": ["2004.01678", "2004.14060", "2006.05880", "2007.02873", "2010.14293", "2011.07812", "2103.04956", "2106.01676", "2109.13808", "2111.08340", "2202.08676", "2207.00348", "2208.12095", "2209.07327", "2211.08028", "2302.05225", "2303.15340", "2307.01094", "2308.02285", "2401.05299", "2402.08486", "2407.10549", "2503.19420", "2506.13565", "2510.07527", "2604.21670", "2604.27044"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2407.10549"], "