{"run_id": "20260817T144023-hepkg-49061", "qid": "gen-paper-dfbb7561", "repeat": 2, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "88358778a0b0", "git_sha": "91aeb1c-dirty", "question": "Which observables does analysis 2009.04363 measure?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "The graph does not record which observables analysis 2009.04363 measures. This could mean that the paper does not explicitly state the observables it measures, or that the information is not captured in the current version of the graph. If you need this information, you might want to check the original paper directly.", "answered": false, "papers": [], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2009.04369"], "predicate": "result_measures_observable"}, "rows": 0, "error": null, "seconds": 0.031}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": [], "evidence_ids": [], "seen_values": [], "verification_score": 0.0, "unsupported_claims": ["2009.04363"], "llm_calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 8936, "completion_tokens": 210, "rounds": 2, "seconds": 8.298737001605332, "reviews": [], "recovered_calls": 0, "cited": "", "abstention_challenged": false, "citation_corrected": false, "citation_disagrees": [], "invented_ids": [], "nudged": false, "error": ""}, "scores": {"seconds": 8.298737001605332, "llm_calls": 2.0, "tokens": 9146.0, "rounds": 2.0, "errored": 0.0, "answered": 0.0, "abstained": 1.0, "refused_in_text": 1.0, "refusal_flag_disagrees": 0.0, "faithfulness": 0.0, "unsupported_claims": 1.0, "retrieved_label_recall": 0.0, "retrieved_entities": 0.0, "mentioned_label_recall": 0.0, "truncation_loss_labels": 0.0, "tool_calls": 1.0, "tool_errors": 0.0, "tool_error_rate": 0.0, "retrieved_first": 1.0, "entities_retrieved": 0.0, "evidence_quotes": 0.0}}
{"run_id": "20260817T144023-hepkg-49061", "qid": "gen-paper-e215b6d1", "repeat": 2, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "88358778a0b0", "git_sha": "91aeb1c-dirty", "question": "How many simulated samples does analysis 2012.08600 use?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "Analysis 2012.08600 uses 5 simulated samples:\n\n- BSM signal samples (MadGraph5_aMC@NLO, LO, up to 2 additional partons)\n- DY+jets and photon+jets samples (MadGraph5_aMC@NLO, LO, up to 4 additional partons)\n- WW, qq->ZZ, ttbar, and single top samples (POWHEG, NLO)\n- gg->ZZ sample (MCFM 7.0, LO)\n- ttV and VVV samples (MadGraph5_aMC@NLO, NLO)\n\nThis information is supported by the following verbatim quotes from the paper:\n\n- \"BSM signal samples were generated using MadGraph5_aMC@NLO at leading order (LO) with up to 2 additional partons.\"\n- \"DY+jets and photon+jets samples were generated using MadGraph5_aMC@NLO at leading order (LO) with up to 4 additional partons.\"\n- \"WW, qq→ZZ, tt̄, and single top samples were generated using POWHEG at next-to-leading order (NLO).\"\n- \"gg→ZZ sample was generated using MCFM 7.0 at leading order (LO).\"\n- \"ttV and VVV samples were generated using MadGraph5_aMC@NLO at next-to-leading order (NLO).\"\n\nTherefore, the analysis uses 5 distinct simulated samples.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2012.08600"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2012.08600"], "predicate": "result_uses_sample"}, "rows": 5, "error": null, "seconds": 0.035}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:sample:dy_photon_jets_madgraph", "hepkg:sample:gg_zz_mcfm", "hepkg:sample:signal_bsm_madgraph", "hepkg:sample:ttv_vvv_madgraph", "hepkg:sample:ww_zz_ttbar_singletop_powheg"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:02a28f1c023f1b7a9c0b3941", "hepkg:evidence:5c2068270153de461c923369", "hepkg:evidence:65dcc4e2b5e7689f8cebc64b", "hepkg:evidence:88df0881fb92b68f94a00a74", "hepkg:evidence:a64063ea479fd9e98592497d"], "seen_values": ["2", "2012.086", "2012.08600", "4", "7", "7.0", "additional", "and", "bsm", "gg-", "hepkg:sample:dy_photon_jets_madgraph", "hepkg:sample:gg_zz_mcfm", "hepkg:sample:signal_bsm_madgraph", "hepkg:sample:ttv_vvv_madgraph", "hepkg:sample:ww_zz_ttbar_singletop_powheg", "jets", "madgraph5_amc", "mcfm", "nlo", "partons", "photon", "powheg", "qq-", "result_uses_sample", "sample", "samples", "signal", "single", "top", "ttbar", "ttv", "vvv"], "verification_score": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": [], "llm_calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 9315, "completion_tokens": 702, "rounds": 2, "seconds": 27.260121954604983, "reviews": [], "recovered_calls": 0, "cited": "", "abstention_challenged": false, "citation_corrected": false, "citation_disagrees": [], "invented_ids": [], "nudged": false, "error": ""}, "scores": {"seconds": 27.260121954604983, "llm_calls": 2.0, "tokens": 10017.0, "rounds": 2.0, "errored": 0.0, "answered": 1.0, "abstained": 0.0, "refused_in_text": 0.0, "refusal_flag_disagrees": 0.0, "faithfulness": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": 0.0, "count_correct": 1.0, "tool_calls": 1.0, "tool_errors": 0.0, "tool_error_rate": 0.0, "retrieved_first": 1.0, "entities_retrieved": 5.0, "evidence_quotes": 5.0}}
{"run_id": "20260817T144023-hepkg-49061", "qid": "gen-paper-e37afe2a", "repeat": 2, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "88358778a0b0", "git_sha": "91aeb1c-dirty", "question": "How many physics processes does analysis 2106.01676 target?", "shape": "count", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "easy", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2106.01676 targets 3 physics processes:\n\n1. **chi1(pm) chi2(0) pair production, Wh-mediated decay to two chi1(0) LSPs, 3-lepton final state**\n2. **chi1(pm) chi2(0) pair production, off-shell W*Z*-mediated decay to two chi1(0) LSPs, 3-lepton final state**\n3. **chi1(pm) chi2(0) pair production, on-shell WZ-mediated decay to two chi1(0) LSPs, 3-lepton final state**\n\nThese processes are detailed in the paper.", "answered": true, "papers": ["2106.01676"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2106.01676"], "predicate": "result_targets_process"}, "rows": 3, "error": null, "seconds": 0.038}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:process:c1c2-Wh-3l", "hepkg:process:c1c2-offshellWZ-3l", "hepkg:process:c1c2-onshellWZ-3l"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:42444cc6d859a4a60417b03b", "hepkg:evidence:7f16a84ba10ce6c38a6dfed4", "hepkg:evidence:821e883d9439fa0d566061dd", "hepkg:evidence:946ae236e2e9f8e7eb886f0f", "hepkg:evidence:b6af06b694789ac23bd665f3", "hepkg:evidence:b9a5109df1af09c3e3c3b265", "hepkg:evidence:dd882fb384b2f33be977a81d"], "seen_values": ["-lepton", "-mediated", "0", "2106.01676", "3", "chi1", "chi2", "decay", "final", "hepkg:process:c1c2-offshellwz-3l", "hepkg:process:c1c2-onshellwz-3l", "hepkg:process:c1c2-wh-3l", "lsps", "off-shell", "on-shell", "pair", "physics_process", "production", "result_targets_process", "state", "two", "wh-mediated", "wz-mediated"], "verification_score": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": [], "llm_calls": 2, "prompt_tokens": 9208, "completion_tokens": 364, "rounds": 2, "seconds": 14.196481039747596, "reviews": [], "recovered_calls": 0, "cited": "", "abstention_challenged": false, "citation_corrected": false, "citation_disagrees": [], "invented_ids": [], "nudged": false, "error": ""}, "scores": {"seconds": 14.196481039747596, "llm_calls": 2.0, "tokens": 9572.0, "rounds": 2.0, "errored": 0.0, "answered": 1.0, "abstained": 0.0, "refused_in_text": 0.0, "refusal_flag_disagrees": 0.0, "faithfulness": 1.0, "unsupported_claims": 0.0, "count_correct": 1.0, "tool_calls": 1.0, "tool_errors": 0.0, "tool_error_rate": 0.0, "retrieved_first": 1.0, "entities_retrieved": 3.0, "evidence_quotes": 7.0}}
{"run_id": "20260817T144023-hepkg-49061", "qid": "gen-paper-e588a3a8", "repeat": 2, "system": "hepkg", "config_hash": "88358778a0b0", "git_sha": "91aeb1c-dirty", "question": "Which statistical methods does analysis 2602.18611 use?", "shape": "set", "split": "dev", "needs": ["sql"], "difficulty": "medium", "answer": {"text": "The analysis 2602.18611 uses the following statistical methods:\n\n- Asimov data set method for expected results\n- Asymptotic approximation for 68%/95% CL intervals (q<1, q<3.84; q<2.30, q<5.99 for 2D)\n- Barlow-Beeston lite approach for MC statistical uncertainties in simulated templates\n- CMS Combine statistical analysis tool (RooFit/RooStats)\n- Correlation matrix extraction from second derivatives of q(alpha) around best fit\n- Maximum likelihood fits to extract SMEFT Wilson coefficient constraints\n- Moment matching procedure to determine simplified-likelihood parameters (dimidated Gaussian)\n- Principal component analysis (PCA) of Hessian matrix to derive constrained SMEFT eigenvector directions\n- Profile likelihood ratio test statistic q(alpha)\n- SM compatibility p-value from chi-square distribution of q(alpha_SM)\n- Simplified likelihood procedure (Gaussian/dimidated-Gaussian approximation) for SMEFT constraints\n\nThese methods are used to perform the statistical analysis in the paper.\n\n<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"answer\", \"arguments\": {\"text\": \"The analysis 2602.18611 uses the following statistical methods:\\n\\n- Asimov data set method for expected results\\n- Asymptotic approximation for 68%/95% CL intervals (q<1, q<3.84; q<2.30, q<5.99 for 2D)\\n- Barlow-Beeston lite approach for MC statistical uncertainties in simulated templates\\n- CMS Combine statistical analysis tool (RooFit/RooStats)\\n- Correlation matrix extraction from second derivatives of q(alpha) around best fit\\n- Maximum likelihood fits to extract SMEFT Wilson coefficient constraints\\n- Moment matching procedure to determine simplified-likelihood parameters (dimidated Gaussian)\\n- Principal component analysis (PCA) of Hessian matrix to derive constrained SMEFT eigenvector directions\\n- Profile likelihood ratio test statistic q(alpha)\\n- SM compatibility p-value from chi-square distribution of q(alpha_SM)\\n- Simplified likelihood procedure (Gaussian/dimidated-Gaussian approximation) for SMEFT constraints\", \"answerable\": true, \"reason\": \"answered\"}}}\n</tool_call>", "answered": true, "papers": ["2602.18611"], "value": null, "steps": [{"round": 1, "tool": "contents_of", "args": {"paper_ids": ["2602.18611"], "predicate": "result_uses_statistical_method"}, "rows": 11, "error": null, "seconds": 0.037}], "sets": {}, "entity_ids": ["hepkg:method:barlow_beeston_lite", "hepkg:statistical_method:asimov_dataset_method", "hepkg:statistical_method:asymptotic_approximation_cl_intervals", "hepkg:statistical_method:combine_roofit_roostats_tool", "hepkg:statistical_method:hessian_correlation_extraction", "hepkg:statistical_method:maximum_likelihood_fit_smeft", "hepkg:statistical_method:moment_matching_procedure", "hepkg:statistical_method:pca_hessian_smeft", "hepkg:statistical_method:profile_likelihood_ratio_test_statistic", "hepkg:statistical_method:simplified_likelihood_procedure", "hepkg:statistical_method:sm_compatibility_pvalue"], "evidence_ids": ["hepkg:evidence:0991129494c227759ba613c8", "hepkg:evidence:27ae94fc7c16fc9385a27c50", "hepkg:evidence:2865d13800143e68107c7de4", "hepkg:evidence:5281bde2c76a4d07d7e3e116", "hepkg:evidence:68da6d6f01610bcc4d79d21c", "hepkg:evidence:8320527288c25fd4c663533f", "hepkg:evidence:a78ed551d48a0e3e5a65834d", "hepkg:evidence:f1e5d084946e132c1483a200", "hepkg:evidence:f6bd443234f00466c1c5eb75", "hepkg:evidence:fe1a8cc65b2c41e95f7a80c7"], "seen_values": ["1", "2", "2.3", "2.30", "2602.18611", "3.84", "5.99", "68", "95", "alpha", "alpha_sm", "analysis", "approach", "approximation", "around", "asimov", "asymptotic", "background_method", "barlow-beeston", "best", "chi-square", "cms", "coeffi